      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, but it feels like you're saying tradition only matters if it fits a certain modern mold. so if a tradition doesn't pass that \"modern ethical lens\" test, it's basically just dismissed? it seems like you're prioritizing a specific progressive way of looking at the world over the actual value that tradition holds for people. how would you define a virtue for someone who believes protecting cultural continuity is more important than constant social change?",
